00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:00.710
that maybe earth isn't the
trash fire she thought it was.

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:02.130
It's gonna be a rough journey for her

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.190
when she becomes a human

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:04.990
and realizes that she's now more kindling

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:07.500
for the org shaped trash
fire, we all live on.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:09.520
Maybe the best case for this movie

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.540
is accidentally super
philosophical is in this moment.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.340
After Joe's gig, when he feels empty

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:15.820
and tells Dorothea about it.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:18.580
In response, she tells a
story about a young fish

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.230
who was looking for the ocean.

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:22.400
- The ocean says the older fish.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.060
That's what she's in right now.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:25.830
This? Says the young fish.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.240
This is water.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.500
What I want is the ocean.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:32.970
- In a sense Joe has closed
himself off from existence,

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:34.300
the ocean in the metaphor,

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:37.410
by his preoccupation with the
immediate water around him.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:39.590
He's limited his perspective so much

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.600
that he hasn't considered that happiness

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:43.950
and meaning might exist off stage.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:46.030
So while it might not
have been intentional,

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:49.220
though who knows, maybe
Pixar has a full room

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:51.320
of dusty old German philosophy books.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.160
This part of the film
is actually pretty deep.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.150
Joe's journey isn't
just about figuring out

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.180
what sort of job he wants but rather

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.100
it's one that leads to an interrogation

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.340
about the very nature of existence.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:03.890
It's heavy stuff, and while in the film,

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.690
Joe has an extra lives he inherited

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:07.140
from his brief stint as a cat,

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.890
philosophers like Heidegger
emphasize that our lives

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:12.700
are finite and if we're
not going to live forever

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:15.660
reckoning with these existential
questions really matters

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.603
if we wanna live an authentic life.

00:12:17.603 --> 00:12:20.480
So yeah, pretty, pretty deep.

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:21.850
Finally, let's consider a theme

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:23.700
that's at play throughout the whole film.

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:25.560
Jazz, so as 22 refers to it.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:26.780
- We are jazzing.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.570
- Haha, okay jazzing

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.670
- Rather than a mere
excuse to fill the movie

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:31.990
with amazing music.

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:34.230
Jazz can be understood
as a conceptual motif

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:35.900
that brings all thing together.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.720
Unlike most music you might
see at a concert, you know

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:41.750
when those existed, jazz
places a strong emphasis

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:43.280
on improvisation, in short,

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.960
anyone who has seen a guitar solo

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.780
may have experienced musical improv

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:49.980
but jazz musicians famously
make a point of winging it

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.770
over complicated chord changes.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:54.890
Kind of like when Joe is
thrown into his audition.

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.220
In this way jazz is more

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:59.240
like the experience of human
existence than pop music.

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:02.180
Musicians are free to explore
where the music takes them

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:04.380
rather than strictly
following sheet music.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.830
So when 22 refers to her experience

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.630
of being human as jazzing,

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:10.970
it's not just a cute misuse of a term,

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.990
but an apt analogy for
existing in the world.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:15.270
And of course it makes sense

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.960
that a film exploring
existential themes would use jazz

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:19.640
as its unifying motif.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.420
Much like how jazz is a reaction

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:23.630
to stuffy musical conventions.

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:25.180
Existentialism is a reaction

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:27.810
against the rigid structure
of modern philosophy

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:29.980
and a way of thinking that prioritizes

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:32.610
the dynamic nature of
existence over the fixed nature

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:33.870
of ideas and concepts.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.590
And hey, more than one
academic thinks jazz

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.160
and Heidegger form an odd Alliance.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:41.970
This all brings us back
to our original question.

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:44.000
Is Soul deep or dumb?

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.650
When the movie is down on earth

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:47.330
trying to teach us that it doesn't matter

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:48.560
if we get our dream job

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.840
as long as we learn to
like make the most of it

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.650
without acknowledging the real problems

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.400
with the logic of do what you love.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.440
It gets a little dumb.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:57.550
But when we jump up to the grate before

00:13:57.550 --> 00:14:00.810
the film has a lot to say
about the anxieties inherent

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:01.930
to human existence.

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:04.500
And sheds light on the
ways in which taking hold

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:06.290
of our freedom can be a struggle.

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:08.450
And by bringing it all
together under the motif

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:11.360
of jazz improvisation,
Soul has a lot to say

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:14.590
about how the philosophy of
jazz is a really a philosophy

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:17.250
for the existential improvisation of life.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:22.080
So final score deep-ish and
absolutely worth a watch.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:23.470
But what do you guys think?

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.140
Should Joe have stayed a cat forever

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:27.950
and taken advantage of all
the sunspots in his apartment?

